WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:30.296
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:30.566 --> 01:31.551
=Tigers Sniff the Rose=

3
01:31.551 --> 01:33.560
(Based on the novel of the same name by Yiren Kuikui)

4
01:35.660 --> 01:38.260
=Episode 34=

5
01:45.600 --> 01:46.770
We don't have any fine tea to offer.

6
01:47.240 --> 01:47.850
Just something

7
01:48.490 --> 01:49.080
to quench your thirst.

8
01:50.930 --> 01:51.600
You handle that well.

9
01:54.240 --> 01:55.010
I've done this every day.

10
01:55.570 --> 01:56.320
I get used to it.

11
02:30.530 --> 02:32.690
(So you knew what the poison would do to you.)

12
02:34.320 --> 02:35.880
(That's why you wouldn't listen to me)

13
02:38.200 --> 02:39.160
(and handed over the ledgers.)

14
03:00.970 --> 03:02.600
Miss, why are you crying?

15
03:11.090 --> 03:12.850
It's been dry for so long. The wind carries dust.

16
03:13.480 --> 03:14.370
It keeps blowing right into the eyes.

17
03:15.160 --> 03:16.320
My eyes have been itching too.

18
03:17.410 --> 03:19.760
Then why doesn't she ever speak?

19
03:24.290 --> 03:25.090
My maid

20
03:25.810 --> 03:26.370
can't speak.

21
03:27.480 --> 03:28.010
You know,

22
03:28.530 --> 03:29.290
things are different now.

23
03:29.920 --> 03:30.600
In the palace,

24
03:31.440 --> 03:33.090
we can only trust servants who can't speak

25
03:33.530 --> 03:34.160
to attend to us.

26
03:35.160 --> 03:36.640
Mr. Yan can't see.

27
03:37.130 --> 03:38.530
This young lady can see,

28
03:38.640 --> 03:39.970
but she can't speak.

29
03:40.290 --> 03:41.090
How unfortunate.

30
03:41.970 --> 03:42.440
Miss,

31
03:42.880 --> 03:43.880
can you read?

32
03:46.880 --> 03:48.010
So you can read.

33
03:51.920 --> 03:52.640
Mind your manners.

34
03:54.040 --> 03:54.530
I'm sorry.

35
03:54.760 --> 03:55.160
Magistrate.

36
03:55.640 --> 03:57.480
The well-diggers from east town are here asking for their pay.

37
04:00.290 --> 04:00.880
Please wait here.

38
04:01.530 --> 04:02.370
I'll be right back.

39
04:38.200 --> 04:38.570
I...

40
04:38.880 --> 04:39.250
That's enough.

41
04:40.490 --> 04:41.050
You don't have to say it.

42
04:42.080 --> 04:42.840
I know what you mean.

43
04:43.440 --> 04:44.080
What do you know?

44
04:44.610 --> 04:45.320
You're going to say

45
04:46.440 --> 04:48.050
your old flame is noble

46
04:48.370 --> 04:49.010
and honest,

47
04:49.760 --> 04:50.960
and he'd never embezzle

48
04:51.250 --> 04:52.050
the relief funds in Lanyang.

49
04:52.610 --> 04:52.930
So

50
04:53.440 --> 04:54.320
we have nothing to worry about.

51
04:54.610 --> 04:55.610
Let's go back to Sheng'an.

52
04:56.010 --> 04:56.610
Yang Si.

53
05:00.730 --> 05:01.400
You mean

54
05:02.810 --> 05:03.570
you want to stay here?

55
05:04.370 --> 05:05.200
Lanyang is hit hard by drought.

56
05:06.880 --> 05:07.880
No water for the spring planting.

57
05:08.690 --> 05:09.960
Shouldn't I stay here

58
05:10.610 --> 05:11.880
and see how he governs,

59
05:12.760 --> 05:14.520
and how the people here live?

60
05:16.880 --> 05:18.320
I'll stay a few more days.

61
05:21.280 --> 05:21.810
What else

62
05:22.400 --> 05:24.370
would you have me do for you, Your Highness?

63
05:25.050 --> 05:25.570
Convince him

64
05:26.760 --> 05:27.490
to let us stay.

65
05:35.170 --> 05:35.960
You're staying here?

66
05:37.080 --> 05:39.200
Can't old friends share a room and talk late into the night?

67
05:41.320 --> 05:42.570
Yang Si, you're welcome

68
05:43.170 --> 05:43.880
to stay.

69
05:44.490 --> 05:45.050
But

70
05:45.730 --> 05:46.760
my place is rather humble.

71
05:47.280 --> 05:48.050
You might not be comfortable here.

72
05:48.490 --> 05:49.610
I'm not picky.

73
05:50.400 --> 05:52.370
Back when I was in the army, I slept in dirt pits

74
05:52.610 --> 05:53.520
and huddled in snowdrifts.

75
05:54.440 --> 05:55.050
To be honest,

76
05:55.570 --> 05:56.880
I'm worried about the disaster.

77
05:57.640 --> 05:59.370
I'd like to stay and see how the people here are doing,

78
05:59.840 --> 06:02.080
and how you're handling your post as magistrate.

79
06:03.760 --> 06:04.570
I see.

80
06:06.050 --> 06:07.440
You've long been at the heart of power.

81
06:07.930 --> 06:08.880
It's good you came down

82
06:09.370 --> 06:09.730
here.

83
06:10.930 --> 06:11.440
But

84
06:12.250 --> 06:13.280
the drought has been severe lately.

85
06:14.050 --> 06:15.280
I'm spread pretty thin right now.

86
06:15.930 --> 06:16.690
Hope

87
06:17.250 --> 06:19.170
you don't mind the poor hospitality.

88
06:19.610 --> 06:20.370
Of course not.

89
06:21.080 --> 06:22.080
Come on, Shang.

90
06:22.520 --> 06:23.810
Do you take me for some spoiled brat?

91
06:38.840 --> 06:39.440
Good morning, Miss.

92
06:39.840 --> 06:41.280
Mr. Yan has already gone out.

93
06:45.810 --> 06:46.440
Don't worry.

94
06:46.690 --> 06:48.059
He went to deliver water to Mr. Sun

95
06:48.101 --> 06:49.101
in the alley across the street.

96
06:49.690 --> 06:50.490
He's an old man with no family.

97
06:50.640 --> 06:51.810
Mr. Yan has been bringing him water for three years.

98
06:51.960 --> 06:53.250
He knows the way by heart.

99
06:58.170 --> 06:59.130
Are you asking me?

100
07:00.370 --> 07:01.640
There's a charity school next door.

101
07:01.840 --> 07:03.149
Mr. Yan pays an old scholar out of his own salary

102
07:03.191 --> 07:04.421
to teach us to read and write.

103
07:04.730 --> 07:05.760
He's got quite a few students.

104
07:06.370 --> 07:07.280
I should go help.

105
07:07.840 --> 07:08.610
See you later, Miss.

106
07:18.840 --> 07:19.730
Eat up.

107
07:20.010 --> 07:20.640
- Come back for more. - Alright.

108
07:20.760 --> 07:21.179
Come again next time.

109
07:21.221 --> 07:21.861
Come on, man.

110
07:22.340 --> 07:24.110
(County Office)

111
07:24.170 --> 07:25.170
Come back for more if you need it.

112
07:26.280 --> 07:27.250
Did you bring all the tools?

113
07:27.760 --> 07:28.059
Yes.

114
07:28.101 --> 07:28.951
We can eat our fill.

115
07:29.250 --> 07:29.789
We can finally eat our fill.

116
07:29.831 --> 07:31.239
Don't rush, everyone. There's enough for all.

117
07:31.280 --> 07:32.119
No rush. Everyone will get some.

118
07:32.161 --> 07:33.471
There's enough for everyone. Here you go.

119
07:33.570 --> 07:35.400
Good thing the imperial grain shipment arrived.

120
07:35.490 --> 07:36.130
Easy there, ma'am.

121
07:36.840 --> 07:37.690
Come back for more, ma'am.

122
07:39.010 --> 07:39.880
Thank heaven!

123
07:40.010 --> 07:41.490
It's rice. It's really rice!

124
07:42.370 --> 07:42.939
There's enough for all.

125
07:42.981 --> 07:43.901
There's enough for everyone.

126
07:49.690 --> 07:50.440
Easy, man.

127
07:50.730 --> 07:51.840
Easy there. There's plenty.

128
07:52.320 --> 07:53.059
There's plenty.

129
07:53.101 --> 07:55.101
If we'd had a drought like this a few years ago,

130
07:55.610 --> 07:57.810
this city would've been overrun with bandits by now.

131
07:58.370 --> 08:00.440
With Magistrate Yan here, no one has to go hungry.

132
08:00.840 --> 08:03.280
The County Office has also given every household grain and seeds.

133
08:03.640 --> 08:04.880
Lanyang won't fall into chaos.

134
08:05.050 --> 08:05.370
Right.

135
08:05.610 --> 08:06.760
Times are tough,

136
08:06.930 --> 08:08.050
but we'll get through them.

137
08:08.200 --> 08:09.130
That's for sure.

138
08:11.280 --> 08:12.610
What's the point of fixing all this?

139
08:13.520 --> 08:14.280
You sure talk too much.

140
08:14.760 --> 08:16.250
Just listen to Magistrate Yan.

141
08:17.050 --> 08:18.010
If we don't fix it now,

142
08:18.170 --> 08:19.370
it'll be too late once the rain comes.

143
08:20.050 --> 08:20.490
That's right.

144
08:20.960 --> 08:22.810
If Magistrate Yan hadn't taught us to store water,

145
08:23.080 --> 08:24.520
we wouldn't have made it

146
08:24.810 --> 08:25.880
through a drought this bad.

147
08:26.250 --> 08:26.960
Magistrate!

148
08:28.250 --> 08:28.930
Magistrate!

149
08:31.130 --> 08:31.440
Thank you.

150
08:31.930 --> 08:32.640
Magistrate!

151
08:34.520 --> 08:35.210
Magistrate!

152
08:35.760 --> 08:36.330
Magistrate.

153
08:36.680 --> 08:37.829
My mother and the neighbors

154
08:37.871 --> 08:38.941
made these shoes for you.

155
08:39.490 --> 08:41.450
They said Cai returned the wheat seeds.

156
08:41.880 --> 08:42.730
Thank you so much.

157
08:43.160 --> 08:44.010
I don't have anything else to offer.

158
08:44.160 --> 08:45.069
Hope you'll accept them.

159
08:45.111 --> 08:45.701
You don't have to...

160
08:48.520 --> 08:49.040
Thank you.

161
08:51.730 --> 08:52.330
Magistrate!

162
08:52.850 --> 08:53.450
Magistrate!

163
08:53.920 --> 08:54.370
Magistrate!

164
08:55.090 --> 08:55.450
Magistrate.

165
08:56.160 --> 08:57.250
There's trouble at the water sump south of town.

166
08:57.330 --> 08:58.400
They want you to settle the dispute.

167
08:58.610 --> 08:58.920
Hurry.

168
08:59.450 --> 08:59.920
Take me there.

169
09:00.760 --> 09:01.250
Careful, Magistrate.

170
10:04.540 --> 10:06.380
(Slipshod farming ruins the crops; careless weeding spoils the harvest.)

171
11:30.800 --> 11:31.280
Yang Si,

172
11:32.040 --> 11:32.800
why are you still up?

173
11:37.040 --> 11:37.730
So it's not Yang Si.

174
11:38.880 --> 11:40.280
You're the young lady?

175
11:47.250 --> 11:48.040
Thank you, Miss.

176
11:49.400 --> 11:50.010
It's late.

177
11:50.370 --> 11:50.850
You should

178
11:51.680 --> 11:52.640
get some rest.

179
12:25.130 --> 12:26.250
Sorry to trouble you, Miss.

180
12:27.490 --> 12:29.040
May I know your name?

181
12:35.640 --> 12:37.040
(I forgot she couldn't speak.)

182
12:55.210 --> 12:56.370
Zhaoniang?

183
13:14.130 --> 13:14.560
Miss,

184
13:15.210 --> 13:15.920
it's late and the dew is heavy.

185
13:16.880 --> 13:17.970
You should get some rest.

186
13:18.640 --> 13:20.010
I can manage the writing myself.

187
13:20.880 --> 13:21.560
You needn't trouble yourself.

188
13:29.330 --> 13:29.970
Alright.

189
13:30.610 --> 13:31.400
Go ahead, Miss.

190
13:59.060 --> 14:02.520
♪The midsummer breeze blows soft and sweet♪

191
14:03.260 --> 14:06.720
♪Fireflies dance freely through the night♪

192
14:07.560 --> 14:11.120
♪Chasing the beauty of this fleeting world♪

193
14:11.660 --> 14:15.090
♪A thousand lights turn night into day♪

194
14:15.920 --> 14:19.620
♪Cicada songs mingle with the wine♪

195
14:20.260 --> 14:24.060
♪Their songs linger through the passing years♪

196
14:24.520 --> 14:28.090
♪Life is but a fleeting stay♪

197
14:28.520 --> 14:31.110
♪How lucky I am to walk this path with you♪

198
14:31.160 --> 14:31.560
Thank you.

199
14:33.090 --> 14:36.690
♪Playing out life's game, forever by your side♪

200
14:37.320 --> 14:40.960
♪Innocent years drift gently by♪

201
14:41.620 --> 14:45.160
♪I thought time might stand still♪

202
14:45.320 --> 14:48.626
♪Forever at that crossroads♪

203
14:48.700 --> 14:50.740
(Pray for rain)

204
14:50.782 --> 14:53.760
♪Watching flowers bloom and fade♪

205
14:54.360 --> 14:57.920
♪Weathering life's rise and fall♪

206
14:58.660 --> 15:01.960
♪So wordless tenderness♪

207
15:02.660 --> 15:06.420
♪Is starlight caught in your eyes♪

208
15:07.220 --> 15:10.860
♪Watching flowers bloom and fade♪

209
15:11.460 --> 15:14.860
♪Weathering life's rise and fall♪

210
15:15.690 --> 15:19.060
♪So wordless tenderness♪

211
15:19.720 --> 15:23.560
♪Is starlight caught in your eyes♪

212
15:48.620 --> 15:51.780
(When the sun or moon is eclipsed, we save it.)

213
15:58.360 --> 16:02.090
♪When the evening breeze begins to blow♪

214
16:03.120 --> 16:05.820
♪After the letter arrives and the words are said♪

215
16:06.890 --> 16:10.440
♪In my dreams, it's still that same glance♪

216
16:10.490 --> 16:11.040
Thank you.

217
16:11.160 --> 16:14.460
♪From the day we first met♪

218
16:15.420 --> 16:19.020
♪A blush of rouge fills my sleeves♪

219
16:19.760 --> 16:23.320
♪I climb the tower time and again♪

220
16:23.960 --> 16:27.490
♪The waters flow; the moon hangs like a hook♪

221
16:28.060 --> 16:31.620
♪And so it lasts forever♪

222
16:32.690 --> 16:36.020
♪Though we're worlds apart, our hearts stay close♪

223
16:36.820 --> 16:40.360
♪Innocent years drift gently by♪

224
16:41.060 --> 16:44.720
♪I wish time could stand still♪

225
16:44.820 --> 16:48.690
♪Forever at that crossroads♪

226
16:49.560 --> 16:53.320
♪Watching flowers bloom and fade♪

227
16:53.820 --> 16:57.220
♪Weathering life's rise and fall♪

228
16:58.120 --> 17:01.420
♪Where endless time comes to an end♪

229
17:02.120 --> 17:05.690
♪Moonlight and breeze fill our boat home♪

230
17:06.660 --> 17:10.020
♪Golden winds and jade dew return♪

231
17:10.920 --> 17:14.460
♪The world still blooms as before♪

232
17:15.120 --> 17:18.660
♪How lucky to roam with you♪

233
17:18.710 --> 17:22.800
♪Back to the road where it all began♪

234
17:23.760 --> 17:27.020
♪As if our youthful hearts remain♪

235
17:28.060 --> 17:31.560
♪As if our love will never fade♪

236
17:32.220 --> 17:38.020
♪Chasing clouds by boat, carefree and unbound♪

237
18:20.890 --> 18:21.360
Father.

238
18:22.040 --> 18:22.890
You're awake.

239
18:32.320 --> 18:33.520
What are you doing here?

240
18:39.120 --> 18:40.989
Father, I missed you.

241
18:41.031 --> 18:42.301
So... so...

242
18:43.170 --> 18:44.930
I brought your grandson to see you.

243
18:53.250 --> 18:55.149
Why did you bring him here?

244
18:55.191 --> 18:56.671
He might catch an illness.

245
18:58.210 --> 19:00.250
Your Majesty, all you have is imperial grace.

246
19:00.520 --> 19:01.360
There's no illness to catch.

247
19:03.450 --> 19:03.730
Come on.

248
19:04.280 --> 19:04.730
Call him Grandfather.

249
19:05.120 --> 19:05.520
Grandfather.

250
19:19.320 --> 19:20.210
Good boy.

251
19:24.170 --> 19:26.930
Your Highness, what's his childhood name?

252
19:27.600 --> 19:28.450
Si'er.

253
19:28.890 --> 19:29.730
Si'er?

254
19:30.840 --> 19:31.120
Come here.

255
19:32.040 --> 19:33.120
Let Grandfather have a good look.

256
19:34.560 --> 19:34.840
Come on.

257
19:35.120 --> 19:36.210
Sit up here on me.

258
19:41.800 --> 19:42.739
Let me see.

259
19:42.781 --> 19:44.671
What's that you're playing with?

260
19:45.170 --> 19:46.730
It's a conch.

261
19:48.320 --> 19:49.170
Your Majesty,

262
19:49.800 --> 19:50.800
you look better

263
19:51.040 --> 19:52.690
than ever today.

264
19:53.730 --> 19:54.650
Your Highnesses,

265
19:55.080 --> 19:57.010
you really should bring the little one more often.

266
20:01.360 --> 20:01.800
Si'er.

267
20:02.520 --> 20:03.600
Say Grandfather again.

268
20:04.280 --> 20:04.690
Grandfather!

269
20:07.890 --> 20:08.800
Look at those little hands.

270
20:10.450 --> 20:11.250
So chubby.

271
20:33.560 --> 20:34.490
What's that sound?

272
20:34.840 --> 20:37.080
The sea. Do you hear the birds?

273
20:40.800 --> 20:41.730
I do.

274
21:09.210 --> 21:10.450
It's been three whole years.

275
21:14.120 --> 21:15.690
Will you still not forgive me?

276
21:19.280 --> 21:20.690
The Princess Consort of Jin didn't deserve to die.

277
21:22.410 --> 21:23.450
She was a pitiful woman too.

278
21:26.800 --> 21:29.120
But for three years, every time I held Si'er,

279
21:32.280 --> 21:33.040
I'd think...

280
21:38.520 --> 21:40.080
you did all this for me.

281
21:44.490 --> 21:45.730
How could I blame you?

282
22:12.690 --> 22:13.120
It's all right.

283
22:15.410 --> 22:15.800
Chunhua.

284
22:19.450 --> 22:20.280
Just seeing you is enough.

285
22:23.690 --> 22:24.040
Even if we

286
22:25.650 --> 22:26.170
stand here in silence,

287
22:30.730 --> 22:31.760
I'm happy.

288
22:49.080 --> 22:50.170
In the few days I've been here,

289
22:51.320 --> 22:52.250
I've been watching

290
22:52.890 --> 22:53.690
and doing the sums.

291
22:55.450 --> 22:56.890
Even if Yan Shang gives it everything,

292
22:58.040 --> 22:59.730
the relief grain Lanyang gets

293
23:00.040 --> 23:00.800
is only so much.

294
23:02.080 --> 23:03.080
It won't last through the eighth month.

295
23:03.410 --> 23:05.120
Aren't you already planning to waive the taxes?

296
23:06.690 --> 23:07.560
Even so,

297
23:08.760 --> 23:09.650
if it doesn't rain soon,

298
23:10.170 --> 23:11.010
there'll be no autumn harvest.

299
23:12.450 --> 23:13.970
The drought stretches so wide.

300
23:14.360 --> 23:15.410
Every region is struggling.

301
23:16.410 --> 23:18.650
Borrowing grain from elsewhere won't work.

302
23:19.890 --> 23:20.560
When that time comes,

303
23:21.730 --> 23:22.890
many people will starve to death.

304
23:23.280 --> 23:23.890
So

305
23:24.890 --> 23:26.080
Lanyang still has no way out?

306
23:26.760 --> 23:27.320
I'm afraid

307
23:28.840 --> 23:29.690
it's not just Lanyang.

308
23:40.080 --> 23:41.010
- Easy there. - Has the physician arrived yet?

309
23:41.170 --> 23:41.650
I'll go hurry him.

310
23:41.890 --> 23:42.210
Okay.

311
23:43.170 --> 23:43.760
What happened?

312
23:44.690 --> 23:45.840
There's only one well left in Lanyang

313
23:46.490 --> 23:47.320
that hasn't dried up.

314
23:48.170 --> 23:50.250
Everyone's been struggling these days.

315
23:51.250 --> 23:52.690
A fight broke out over the well

316
23:53.210 --> 23:54.010
just now.

317
23:55.040 --> 23:55.970
In the past two years,

318
23:56.040 --> 23:58.010
we've hardly had any fights here.

319
23:58.250 --> 23:59.970
It's all this cursed drought!

320
24:00.120 --> 24:01.189
- We can go without water, - Exactly.

321
24:01.231 --> 24:02.471
but the fields can't.

322
24:02.650 --> 24:04.210
Otherwise, we still won't make it to autumn.

323
24:04.360 --> 24:05.099
Still a dead end.

324
24:05.141 --> 24:06.471
That's right.

325
24:07.970 --> 24:09.490
An elder got hurt trying to break up the fight.

326
24:10.280 --> 24:11.490
So we carried him here.

327
24:12.040 --> 24:12.520
Magistrate,

328
24:12.930 --> 24:14.320
I heard you came third in the imperial exams.

329
24:14.560 --> 24:16.890
You're a scholar blessed by the deities.

330
24:17.170 --> 24:18.840
Surely even Heaven will hear you.

331
24:19.170 --> 24:20.490
